Subject: Security Review - Customer Support Portal

Hi Sarah and Rahul,

I've completed the initial security review for the proposed Customer Support Portal.

Most of the functional requirements look good, but I'd like the following security requirements to be included before development begins.

- Customer passwords must never be stored in plain text and should be securely hashed.
- All customer information should be encrypted while stored in the database.
- Support agents and administrators should authenticate using multi-factor authentication.
- Customer accounts can continue using email and password for the first release.
- User sessions should automatically expire after 15 minutes of inactivity.
- Only support agents and administrators should be able to access internal ticket notes.
- All important user actions should be recorded in audit logs for compliance purposes.

I also recommend scheduling automated daily database backups and defining a system availability target before finalizing the BRD.

These requirements should help us satisfy our internal security and compliance standards without significantly impacting the delivery timeline.

Regards,

